media: i2c: imx582: add a 1984x1488 4x4 binned mode of the whole array

The fast 1080p mode reads only 4320 of the array's 6000 rows, so a 4:3
viewfinder from it shows less than a 4000x3000 photo, and the 12 MP mode
as a viewfinder runs at about 15 fps in libcamera's software ISP.  This
mode is the 1080p mode with every row read (Y 0-5999), 1488 of the 1500
binned rows kept (digital crop) and a frame of 1570 lines: about 67 fps,
with the same line length and link frequency.

Not yet run on the phone.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx582.c	2026-11-15 23:39:07.976888756 +0100
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx582.c	2026-11-15 23:39:08.002630184 +0100
@@ -1023,6 +1023,126 @@
 	{ CCI_REG8(0x4035), 0xf0 },
 };
 
